---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Advisory for Buyers & Traders"
  description="Sourcing mandates in the gold and diamond trade, and verifiable answers about origin and chain of custody for buyers and traders sourcing from ASM value chains."
>
  <section class="section service-page">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow"><a href="/what-we-do">&larr; What We Do</a></p>
      <h1 class="reveal">06 &middot; Advisory for Buyers &amp; Traders</h1>
      <p class="lede reveal">
        Buyers and traders sourcing gold and other minerals out of frontier
        markets face growing scrutiny on where material actually comes
        from. We help make that answer solid.
      </p>

      <div class="body-grid">
        <div class="reveal">
          <h2>What this covers</h2>
          <p>
            Sourcing mandates, particularly in the gold and diamond trade:
            we identify and vet supply on a buyer&rsquo;s behalf, drawing on
            our own network of ASM and large-scale contacts across
            Sub-Saharan Africa.
          </p>
          <p>
            Supply chain mapping back to specific mine sites, verification
            of existing sourcing documentation, and gap analysis against
            responsible sourcing frameworks that regulators and downstream
            buyers increasingly ask about.
          </p>
          <p>
            Our blockchain-based traceability approach can be applied
            directly to a buyer&rsquo;s existing supplier relationships,
            turning informal sourcing claims into a documented, auditable
            chain of custody.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="reveal">
          <h2>How we work</h2>
          <p>
            We work with both ends of the relationship: the buyer or
            trader who needs the assurance, and the mine site that has to
            actually produce the records. That dual view is what makes the
            resulting documentation hold up.
          </p>
          <p>
            Where a supplier&rsquo;s practices fall short, we can advise
            them directly on what closing the gap requires, so a sourcing
            relationship can continue on a defensible footing.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="cta-row">
        <a class="pill-btn" href="/contact">Talk to us about your supply chain</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .service-page .eyebrow {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .lede {
    max-width: 720px;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    margin-bottom: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem);
  }

  .body-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: var(--gap);
    margin-bottom: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4rem);
  }

  .cta-row {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    padding-top: 2rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 800px) {
    .body-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
